            "\nIf you are interested in microeconometric analysis of individual and household behavior, you need to understand the role of endogenous and exogenous variables in your models. These variables are crucial for identifying causal effects and estimating parameters of interest. In this article, you will learn what are the differences between endogenous and exogenous variables, how to test for endogeneity, and how to deal with it using various methods.\n",
